> When you die, does everything on the square where you stand go through
> the curse check, or is it only the items in your inventory?

Only what you're carrying.

> I've started to wonder whether just dropping everything on running into
> a fairly hopeless situation (surrounded by mumakil, for instance) might
> not be a bad idea. Encumbrance drops instantly, and if I die, the bones
> file is more useful.

Well, I've never heard of anyone being surrounded by mumakil. Mumakil are
generated as single mosnters, not in groups like rothés.

And I would advise against dropping everything, since that would lose you
a turn which you *really* need right now.

The only exception to this would be when you're encumbered: in that case
you should drop as much as you need to become unencumbered, and nothing
more, since everything you're still carrying may still help you. Of
course, your *real* problem is not that a mumak is beating on you, but
that you were encumbered in the first place, which shouldn't happen. When
you saw that mumak approach, you should have dropped some stuff
immediately and run off in the opposite direction. Mumakil are slower than
an unencumbered player character.

